  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU as Guest of Honor at the Guadalajara International Book Fair (November /December 2023)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The EU has accepted to participate as Guest of Honour (GoH) at the Guadalajara International Book Fair (FIL) at its November/December 2023 edition.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The EU participation as GoH will broaden cultural relations and encourage cooperation and co-creation between the EU, its MS, and the LAC region while supporting global circulation of European cultural works and artists; enhance the EU&#xbf;s role and relevance for LAC and globally, focusing particularly on youth (who make up most of the subcontinent&#xbf;s population); generate strategic public and cultural diplomacy actions that could be a template to reproduce and adapt to other global regions. The selection of writers, intellectuals and artists will represent the diversity (in geography, themes, and gender) and modernity of European literature/arts/thinking. Sustainable development, the green transition and climate change will be important themes. The regional dimension will involve stakeholders beyond Mexico, both internally (EU and MS representations in other LAC countries) and externally (artists, high-level speakers, etc.). Within the current circumstances of war, a powerful statement would be to display the larger &#xbf;European family&#xbf; by including non-EU European participants, such as Ukraine, Georgia, and Moldova.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
